\section*{An ultrafilter-free local criterion for O2-ultrapower embeddability}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
One explicit separable unital full group C*-algebra is claimed to embed into no norm ultrapower of a nonzero unital nuclear algebra, giving a negative instance for O\_2 as well. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} Let
\[
G=\mathbb Z[1/2]^3\rtimes(\operatorname{SL}_3(\mathbb Z)\times\mathbb Z),\qquad (M,k)v=2^kMv,\qquad A=C^*(G).
\]
OpenAI claims that for any nuclear $C^*$-algebra $B$ assumed nonzero and unital, and for any free ultrafilter $\omega$ on $\mathbb N$, a unital embedding $A\hookrightarrow B^\omega$ is impossible. This also excludes $\mathcal O_2^\omega$ as a target. The algebra $A$ is the full group algebra and is separable and unital; $B^\omega=\ell^\infty(\mathbb N,B)/\{(b_n):\lim_\omega\|b_n\|=0\}$ is the norm ultrapower. This addresses nuclear norm-ultrapower embeddings.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 292, 2026-09-23): An ascending HNN construction supplies a property-T base with finite-index self-embeddings. A nuclear tensor-product estimate restricts the finite-dimensional representation types approximated by arbitrary unitary tuples, uniformly in dimension. Applying this to coordinate lifts of a proposed ultrapower embedding and then inducing through the self-embedding produces incompatible finite sets of representation types.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 292, 2026-09-23): The separable unital counterexample cannot embed unitally into \(\mathcal O_2^\omega\); any nonunital embedding sends its unit to a nonzero projection, which is equivalent to 1 coordinatewise in O2, so passing to that corner would give a forbidden unital embedding.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 292, the scope page documents the following selections. The selected full-group algebra has no unital embedding in a norm ultrapower of any nonzero unital nuclear target. In particular, the Cuntz-algebra ultrapower target is excluded. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: NuclearUltrapower.lean. Declarations: OAI.NuclearUltrapower.main\_no\_embedding.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{An explicit obstruction to nuclear norm-ultrapower embeddings}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/An-explicit-obstruction-to-nuclear-norm-ultrapower-embeddings-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex\#L36}{thm:main}.
\item Family 292: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/292.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/NuclearUltrapower.json}{Comparator NuclearUltrapower.json}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/NuclearUltrapower.lean}{Comparator NuclearUltrapower.lean}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/CONTENTS.md}{OpenAI catalogue entry}.
\end{itemize}
